    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0435" n="1395" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1395"/>

                <head>No. 941.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Baron d’Almeirim to Mr.
                    Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Portugal in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-08-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 7, 1888</date>. (Received August
                    8.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: My Government has just
                    instructed me to inform you that the tribes of Quissembo have submitted to the
                    authority of the Government of Portugal, and that the original ground for the
                    blockade having been removed, the blockade itself has therefore been raised, and
                    the port is again opened to the commerce of all the powers.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baron d’Almeirim</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul in Charge of the Business of the Legation of
                            Portugal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
